---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const p='/equipment/16-08/',guide='https://www.eppendorf.com/product-media/doc/en/186591/Eppendorf_Liquid-Handling_Operating-manual_Research-plus_Eppendorf-Research-plus.pdf',model='https://www.eppendorf.com/product-media/doc/en/1118249/Liquid-Handling_Product-note_Research-plus_Reference-2_epTIPS_Change-notification-Article-numbers-mechanical-pipettes-pipette-tips.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Research plus pipette: dry fit and inventory phantom" description="Inspect a metric pipette and move quantity metadata between two inert reference vessels." wide={true}><article class="equipment" id="drypip"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/16-08/">← Equipment 16-08</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#pip-evidence">Reference sheet</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">16-08 / INERT DRY TRAINING PHANTOM</p><h2>One dry move, two balanced entries</h2><p class="eq-lede">Fit the virtual training tip and commit a 25 µL-equivalent move. The source ledger should drop from 100 to 75 and the receiver should rise to 25. An 80-unit request after that should leave both unchanged.</p></header>
<div class="p-cols"><section><h3>Eppendorf Research plus</h3><canvas id="pip-model" aria-label="Orbitable single-channel Research plus pipette, training stand and empty reference vessels"></canvas><p id="pip-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="pip-front">Whole stand / reset view</button><button id="pip-dial">Head and plunger</button><button id="pip-tip">Tip receptor</button><p>The button and stem animate together. Select the 3D plunger to commit a dry move, the yellow dial to cycle presets, or the tip to release it. These are virtual actions, not pipetting instructions.</p></section>
<section><h3>Dry fit and move</h3><label>Model accessory fit<select id="pip-choice"><option value="matched">Compatible training tip</option><option value="other">Unmatched training sleeve</option></select></label><label>Dry displacement setting, µL equivalent<input id="pip-setting" type="number" min="20" max="200" step=".2" value="25"/></label><p id="pip-fit"></p><p id="pip-travel"></p><button id="pip-attach">Fit virtual tip</button><button id="pip-release">Remove virtual tip</button><button id="pip-run">Commit dry ledger move</button><button id="pip-reset">Restore example</button><p id="pip-status" role="status"></p></section></div>
<section><h3>Dry volume and lineage ledger</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Inert source</th><th>Inert receiver</th><th>Latest child ID</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td id="pip-source"></td><td id="pip-destination"></td><td id="pip-lineage"></td></tr></tbody></table><p id="pip-rev"></p><button id="pip-export">Download dry inventory JSON</button><p><a href={p+'example.json'}>Example export</a>. Each successful inventory event has its own revision. Debits and credits share the parent and child IDs. No sample is handled in this exercise.</p></section>
<section id="pip-evidence"><h3>Configuration, geometry and checks</h3><p>Selected configuration: single-channel mechanical Research plus, yellow 20–200 µL, article 3123 000 055. <a href={model}>Eppendorf variant cross-reference</a> and <a href={guide+'#page=13'}>manufacturer drawing, Fig. 3-1, PDF p. 13</a>. The published adjustment increment is 0.2 µL. Housing, nominal tip fit, stand, dry vessels and 2–12 mm teaching stroke are illustrative and not measured product specifications.</p><div class="p-cols"><figure><img alt="Original Research plus stand view" src={p+'station.webp'}/><figcaption>Original modeled single-channel body, display window, lower shaft and dry training stand.</figcaption></figure><figure><img alt="Original Research plus detail of plunger and ejector" src={p+'head.webp'}/><figcaption>Original close-up matching the control grouping in the manufacturer illustration, not a photograph.</figcaption></figure></div><p>The digital ledger only balances dry equivalent displacement. The 3D strokes visualize the selected setting; they do not model pressure, fluid, calibration bias, transient physics or transfer accuracy. No wet, biological or dosing procedures.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>25 from 100</td><td>75 and 25, same linked IDs</td><td>75.0 and 25.0 µL equivalent</td></tr><tr><td>Request 80 from remaining 75</td><td>Reject atomically</td><td>Both entries unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Wrong training sleeve</td><td>No virtual fit</td><td>Rejected</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href={p+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={p+'research-plus.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={p+'dry-transfer.mjs'}>Pure state and actions</a> · <a href={p+'vr.json'}>VR controls and nominal travel</a>. No headset verification claimed.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/16-08/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#drypip .p-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.08fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#drypip section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#drypip :is(input,select,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#drypip label{display:grid;gap:.2rem;min-width:0;margin:.35rem 0}#drypip label :is(input,select){width:100%;min-width:0}#drypip button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#drypip button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#pip-model{display:block;width:100%;height:330px;touch-action:none}#drypip figure{margin:.5rem 0}#drypip figure img{width:100%}#drypip table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;text-align:left}#drypip td,#drypip th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:780px){#drypip .p-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#pip-model{height:280px}}</style>
